<?phem

namespace App\Ui\Demos;

use Phem\Attribute\{Component, Page};
use Phem\Node;

use function App\Ui\{DemoPage, Example, Examples, Hero};
use function Phem\Ui\Base\{AlertDialog, AlertDialogClose, AlertDialogDescription, AlertDialogPayload, AlertDialogPopup, AlertDialogTitle, AlertDialogTrigger, MenuItem, MenuPopup, MenuSeparator, MenuTrigger};
use Phem\Ui\Base\{Align, Menu};

#[Page('/components/alert-dialog')]
function AlertDialogPage(): Node
{
    return (
        <DemoPage slug="alert-dialog">
            <Hero source="AlertDialogHeroDemo">
                <AlertDialogHeroDemo />
            </Hero>
            <Examples>
                <Example title="Open from a menu" source="AlertDialogFromMenuDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>In order to open an alert dialog using a menu, make the menu item a detached trigger of the alert dialog: give it <code>data-phem-dialog-for</code> with the <code>handle</code> of the alert dialog. The click closes the menu and opens the alert dialog.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AlertDialogFromMenuDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Close confirmation" source="DialogCloseConfirmationDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>This example shows a nested confirmation dialog that opens if the text entered in the parent dialog is going to be discarded.</p>
                        <p>To implement this, give the <code>confirmClose</code> prop of the parent <code>Dialog</code> the <code>handle</code> of an <code>AlertDialog</code> in its popup. When the user changed a field, a request to close opens the alert dialog: the confirmation is automatically shown when the user clicks the backdrop, presses the Esc key, or clicks a close button. Its <code>DialogDiscard</code> button closes the two dialogs.</p>
                        <p>Use the <code>[data-nested-dialog-open]</code> selector and the <code>var(--nested-dialogs)</code> CSS variable to customize the styling of the parent dialog. Backdrops of the child dialogs won't be rendered so that you can present the parent dialog in a clean way behind the one on top of it.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <DialogCloseConfirmationDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Detached triggers" source="AlertDialogDetachedDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>An alert dialog can be controlled by a trigger located either inside or outside the <code>AlertDialog</code> component. For simple, one-off interactions, place the <code>AlertDialogTrigger</code> inside <code>AlertDialog</code>, as shown in the example at the top of this page.</p>
                        <p>However, if defining the alert dialog's content next to its trigger is not practical, you can use a detached trigger. This involves placing the <code>AlertDialogTrigger</code> outside of <code>AlertDialog</code> and linking them with the same <code>handle</code>. The root gets the handle as its <code>id</code>, and the trigger gets <code>data-phem-dialog-for</code>.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AlertDialogDetachedDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Multiple triggers" source="AlertDialogMultipleDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>A single alert dialog can be opened by multiple trigger elements. You can achieve this by using the same <code>handle</code> for several detached triggers, or by placing multiple <code>AlertDialogTrigger</code> components inside a single <code>AlertDialog</code>.</p>
                        <p>The alert dialog can render different content depending on which trigger opened it. Give each trigger a <code>payload</code>: the <code>AlertDialogPayload</code> part shows the payload of the trigger that opened the alert dialog.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AlertDialogMultipleDemo />
                </Example>
                <Example title="Controlled mode with multiple triggers" source="AlertDialogControlledDemo">
                    <Example.description>
                        <p>You can control the alert dialog's open state with the <code>defaultOpen</code> and <code>triggerId</code> props of <code>AlertDialog</code>: a render with new values opens the alert dialog for the trigger with that <code>id</code>. The controller keeps the values of the browser in <code>data-phem-dialog-open-value</code> and <code>data-phem-dialog-trigger-id-value</code>.</p>
                        <p>Here, the button is in the root, and opens the alert dialog without a request with the <code>phem-dialog#open</code> action and a <code>triggerId</code> param. With no payload, <code>AlertDialogPayload</code> shows its children.</p>
                    </Example.description>
                    <AlertDialogControlledDemo />
                </Example>
            </Examples>
        </DemoPage>
    );
}

/** The hero: an alert dialog with its trigger in the root. */
#[Component]
function AlertDialogHeroDemo(): Node
{
    return (
        <AlertDialog>
            <AlertDialogTrigger className="text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">Discard draft</AlertDialogTrigger>
            <AlertDialogPopup>
                <div className="flex flex-col gap-1">
                    <AlertDialogTitle>Discard draft?</AlertDialogTitle>
                    <AlertDialogDescription>You can’t undo this action.</AlertDialogDescription>
                </div>
                <div className="flex justify-end gap-3">
                    <AlertDialogClose>Cancel</AlertDialogClose>
                    <AlertDialogClose className="text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">Discard</AlertDialogClose>
                </div>
            </AlertDialogPopup>
        </AlertDialog>
    );
}

/** Open from a menu: the last item is a detached trigger of the alert dialog. */
#[Component]
function AlertDialogFromMenuDemo(): Node
{
    return (
        <div>
            <Menu sideOffset={{ 8 }} align={{ Align.Start }}>
                <MenuTrigger>Playlist</MenuTrigger>
                <MenuPopup>
                    <MenuItem>Play</MenuItem>
                    <MenuItem>Share</MenuItem>
                    <MenuSeparator />
                    <MenuItem data-phem-dialog-for="delete-playlist">Delete…</MenuItem>
                </MenuPopup>
            </Menu>
            <AlertDialog handle="delete-playlist">
                <AlertDialogPopup>
                    <div className="flex flex-col gap-1">
                        <AlertDialogTitle>Delete playlist?</AlertDialogTitle>
                        <AlertDialogDescription>You can't undo this action.</AlertDialogDescription>
                    </div>
                    <div className="flex justify-end gap-3">
                        <AlertDialogClose>Cancel</AlertDialogClose>
                        <AlertDialogClose className="text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">Delete</AlertDialogClose>
                    </div>
                </AlertDialogPopup>
            </AlertDialog>
        </div>
    );
}

/** Detached triggers: the trigger is outside the root, with the same handle. */
#[Component]
function AlertDialogDetachedDemo(): Node
{
    return (
        <div>
            <AlertDialogTrigger handle="discard-draft" className="text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">Discard draft</AlertDialogTrigger>
            <AlertDialog handle="discard-draft">
                <AlertDialogPopup>
                    <div className="flex flex-col gap-1">
                        <AlertDialogTitle>Discard draft?</AlertDialogTitle>
                        <AlertDialogDescription>This action cannot be undone.</AlertDialogDescription>
                    </div>
                    <div className="flex justify-end gap-3">
                        <AlertDialogClose>Cancel</AlertDialogClose>
                        <AlertDialogClose className="text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">Discard</AlertDialogClose>
                    </div>
                </AlertDialogPopup>
            </AlertDialog>
        </div>
    );
}

/** Multiple triggers: two detached triggers of one alert dialog, with a payload each. */
#[Component]
function AlertDialogMultipleDemo(): Node
{
    return (
        <div className="flex gap-2">
            <AlertDialogTrigger handle="multiple-alert-dialog" payload="Trigger 1">Trigger 1</AlertDialogTrigger>
            <AlertDialogTrigger handle="multiple-alert-dialog" payload="Trigger 2">Trigger 2</AlertDialogTrigger>
            <AlertDialog handle="multiple-alert-dialog">
                <AlertDialogPopup>
                    <div className="flex flex-col gap-1">
                        <AlertDialogTitle>Alert dialog</AlertDialogTitle>
                        <AlertDialogDescription>Confirming <AlertDialogPayload /></AlertDialogDescription>
                    </div>
                    <div className="flex justify-end gap-3">
                        <AlertDialogClose>Close</AlertDialogClose>
                    </div>
                </AlertDialogPopup>
            </AlertDialog>
        </div>
    );
}

/** Controlled mode: three triggers in the root, and a button that opens the alert dialog for the second one. */
#[Component]
function AlertDialogControlledDemo(): Node
{
    return (
        <AlertDialog>
            <div className="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2">
                <AlertDialogTrigger id="alert-trigger-1" payload="Discard draft?" className="text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">Discard</AlertDialogTrigger>
                <AlertDialogTrigger id="alert-trigger-2" payload="Delete project?" className="text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">Delete</AlertDialogTrigger>
                <AlertDialogTrigger id="alert-trigger-3" payload="Sign out?">Sign out</AlertDialogTrigger>
                <button type="button" data-action="phem-dialog#open" data-phem-dialog-trigger-id-param="alert-trigger-2" className="flex h-8 items-center justify-center border border-neutral-950 dark:border-white bg-white dark:bg-neutral-950 px-3 text-sm text-neutral-950 dark:text-white hover:bg-neutral-100 dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:-outline-offset-1 focus-visible:outline-neutral-950 dark:focus-visible:outline-white">Open programmatically</button>
            </div>
            <AlertDialogPopup>
                <div className="flex flex-col gap-1">
                    <AlertDialogTitle><AlertDialogPayload>Are you sure?</AlertDialogPayload></AlertDialogTitle>
                    <AlertDialogDescription>This action cannot be undone.</AlertDialogDescription>
                </div>
                <div className="flex justify-end gap-3">
                    <AlertDialogClose>Cancel</AlertDialogClose>
                    <AlertDialogClose className="text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">Confirm</AlertDialogClose>
                </div>
            </AlertDialogPopup>
        </AlertDialog>
    );
}
